From 987e4059af8c6e94f22401c0cc2080cbb89b9afc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: claude <claude@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 7 May 2026 23:28:59 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] gofra: configurable per-packet redundancy
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

New [me] config key `redundancy = K` (default 1, current behavior).
Each TX packet (or USO partition) is sent K times via K different
slots — trades throughput for tail-latency and resilience to single
path/NIC drops.

Conn picks the first slot via existing RR next(now) and chains the
remaining K-1 via new next(cur, now), which steps by a coprime offset
(brute-forced per Conn at startup) chosen so every step changes both
src and dst addr — full path diversity. Bijectivity, src-diversity
and dst-diversity are verified strictly: if no such step exists for a
given (N, M) layout (e.g. M=2 always fails geometrically), we raise()
on startup with a clear message. The chosen step is logged per Conn.

K is validated against every peer's N*M at config load. K=1 skips
the step search entirely; existing setups don't change.

Co-Authored-By: Anton Samokhvalov <anton@samokhvalov.xyz>
